{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 13, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "**A Whirlwind in Japan**\n\nJapan stole my heart in just five days. The journey began in **Tokyo**, where neon lights pulsed under cherry blossoms in full bloom along the Sumida River. I started with classic sights—the towering **Senso-ji Temple** in Asakusa, its red lanterns casting a golden glow, and the buzz of **Shibuya Crossing**, the world’s busiest intersection.\n\nNext, I escaped the city for the serene **Kanazawa**, where geisha districts and samurai history unfolded in quiet canals and the opulent **Kenrokuen Garden**. The delicate art of gold leaf crafting in the **Higashi Chaya District** left me mesmerized.\n\nThen, **Kyoto**—a dream in temples and tea. I wandered **Fushimi Inari’s** endless torii gates at sunrise, sipped matcha in a **zen garden**, and marveled at the golden pavilion of **Kinkaku-ji**, its reflection shimmering on a pond. A late-night alley in **Gion**, lined with lanterns, felt like stepping into a Kabuki play.\n\nThe trip ended in **Osaka**, where street food ruled. Takoyaki and okonomiyaki became my lifeline as I squeezed into the narrow streets of **Dotonbori**, its neon signs flashing in the night.\n\nJapan isn’t just a destination—it’s a brushstroke of contrast: ancient and modern, quiet and vibrant, sacred and playful. And in five days, it made me fall in love with its soul.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.06550939381122589}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.27843376994132996}, {"token": " Wh", "logprob": -0.037113383412361145}, {"token": "irl", "logprob": -0.018043426796793938}, {"token": "wind", "logprob": -4.7801782784517854e-05}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -1.6305687427520752}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -0.5167656540870667}, {"token": "**\n\n", "logprob": -2.49527645111084}, {"token": "Japan", "logprob": -1.4009182453155518}, {"token": " stole", "logprob": -1.1661972999572754}, {"toke